# "Other tiles" in the Add tiles library

When you add a new panel (a page of its own), add it to "Other tiles" in the same change.

- The list is `editor/src/model/otherTiles.ts`, drawn by `EntityLibrary.vue`.
- A panel with no entity (home, bedside, lights) is a catalogue kind in `catalogue/_kinds.yaml`: add its key to `OTHER_TILE_KINDS`.
- A panel over an entity (alarm, weather, thermostat, music, calendar) goes in `PANELS`: `name` ("… panel"), `icon`, the entity `domain`, and `kind` only when the panel is a kind of its own over that entity (`music` over `media_player`). Clicking it adds a `full` tile on the first entity of that domain. It is greyed out when Home Assistant has none. The tile drawer changes the entity.
- The catalogue entry must list `full` in `sizes`.
- `editor/src/model/otherTiles.test.ts` reads the `edgeToEdge` set in `TileBox.kt` and fails when a kind there is in neither list.

## Full-page adds

- `TileSource` (`types.ts`: `entityId`, `kind`, `full`) is the one shape for a new tile, from the library through `EditorLayoutCanvas`, `EditorCanvasSection`, `GridMockup`, `ScreenEditor.add` and `design.addEntity`. Don't reintroduce inline `{ entityId?, kind? }`.
- `newTile` picks the `full` size when `source.full` is set and the catalogue allows it, else the first small size. A drag carries `full` on `Dragged` (`drag.ts`), and `GridMockup.drop` passes it on.
- `ScreenEditor.add` refuses a full tile on a page that already has tiles ("A full-page tile needs a page of its own").
- On a free-form page, `design.addEntity` ignores `full` and adds the entity as a tile node.

